#### 🟡 BUG #16 — Payment screenshot size check uses wrong comparison

**Location:** Line 169
```tsx
while (compressed.length > 50 * 1024 && quality > 0.1) {
```

`compressed` is a base64 data URL string. Its `.length` is the **character count**, not bytes. Base64 encodes ~4/3 bytes per character, so 50 * 1024 bytes ≈ 68267 characters. The comparison `> 50 * 1024` (= 51200 characters) is **too strict** — it rejects images well under 50KB.

**Fix:**
```tsx
// Base64 string length ≈ (bytes * 4/3), so 50KB ≈ 68267 chars
const MAX_B64_CHARS = Math.ceil(50 * 1024 * (4/3));
while (compressed.length > MAX_B64_CHARS && quality > 0.1) {
```

